      "writtenOn": "2018-10-02T17:52:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For big size data reading in a single i2c transaction with the following format,\n\u003cS\u003e\u003cAddr\u003e\u003cW\u003e\u003ccmd0\u003e\u003ccmd1\u003e...\u003ccmd-n\u003e\u003cSr\u003e\u003cAddr\u003e\u003cR\u003e\u003cdata0\u003e...\u003cdata\u003c63\u003e\u003cdata64\u003e...\u003cdata123\u003e\u003cdata124\u003e.....\u003cdata-nnn\u003e\u003cP\u003e.\n\n\u0027Restart\u0027 flag should be set at the beginning of data only once while writing to data_cmd register and only chip_i2c_xfer() knows when to insert this bit.\nAnd \u0027restart_flag\u0027 should be kept outside this function and to avoid defining \u0027restart_flag\u0027 as global, this variable is kept inside chip_i2c_xfer() and passed to this function. \nThis variable can be uint8_t is good enough but ISH is 32bit CPU and 32bit memory access must be more efficient.",
      "parentUuid": "e2120186_758a6b8f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 275,
        "startChar": 5,
