      "writtenOn": "2018-10-13T00:21:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, they are not exclusive in case len \u003d\u003d 1.  \nI think you catch bug. Thank you\n(current Elan device has only \u0027even\u0027 numbers of commands without stop and \u0027repeated Start\u0027 for reading.)\n\nIf \u0027len\u0027 \u003d\u003d 1 (only 1 byte command to write), \u0027DATA_CMD_STOP_VAL\u0027 is still needed.\nI will add following line after line 288 to make code to be more generic.\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\nif (i \u003d\u003d 0) ....     {\n\n\n          if (len \u003d\u003d 1)\n              data_cmd |\u003d DATA_CMD_STOP_VAL;\n}",
      "parentUuid": "3f0af0ff_aa186e51",
      "revId": "487cf0bddfc02c1635380ddebb40b3f6169afc38",
